    {
      "id": "claim_8851f07b352049e4bc9acf8b68a60402",
      "statement": "Status on a SpanCitations is exactly `\"supported\"`, `\"partial\"`, or `\"unsupported\"` and is decided from the best exact citation's answer_coverage component, not from the citation's overall score or from embedding similarity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L111-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e80f28ef4f0ec6920a1825fb35b0c93bffe180fdb111a4f77d9ea3ad8b269b51:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1610-L1633",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0546591f2ac5ef2ec8353fa6d983babe6920c357814b4eae7d76a64a8120f7ff:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f0ec700aabc64e69900e3f74b7fba96d",
      "statement": "The default supported_answer_coverage is 0.6 and the default min_answer_coverage is 0.2. A span is `\"supported\"` only when the best citation's answer_coverage clears supported_answer_coverage and no contradiction fired; otherwise it is `\"partial\"`. A candidate must clear min_answer_coverage on sequential Smith-Waterman coverage or on content-word coverage over the same passage before it becomes a Citation, and stopword-only SW hits do not clear it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1631-L1632",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7f8740af416a899db757b7fff330e87dc0ecf3601353b2b32cc088f0b4526537:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L789-L805",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f6adac6eaace68e81e553db3e591b107c43a92bc61c0eb4b4cdbdc8cd16721a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L58-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:89e52f0b3f45e5ba72f8788cd2f13d412c2d42c8ac7b910e2aa4d2dbb1efce60:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_53d466f526d14c6487c892e659e20e58",
      "statement": "Defaults for the remaining quality gates are min_alignment_score=0, min_final_score=0.0, and min_embedding_similarity=0.3. min_final_score is the weighted citation score that must be cleared for a Citation to be emitted at all; min_embedding_similarity is the cosine threshold for an embedding-only entry to surface as retrieval_support.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L710-L710",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:627908313c07c40846927a314724941b5e15d956565777a33307053b3833217f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L738-L738",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2593f3f72c8362594bdb976139d87792f554ea0b9bf5939f5f99814c759e5a29:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L56-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:131459b1f7a5ee1fb195ce547c185e3ed80bc308f2ac18145f1a4fda4a5c5435:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9c4bd9897e7246fe88e001e9753804ca",
      "statement": "top_k defaults to 3 and is the maximum exact citations returned per answer span; max_citations_per_source defaults to 2 and caps how many citations any one source contributes per span; max_retrieval_support defaults to 3 and is the independent cap on retrieval_support entries per span.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1523-L1550",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0941c75e7229f912c66590a2dc6339900ad275856f1c5643f833589af8453761:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1553-L1568",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:afc8f24be114b3b9984600846936361bea90408496d700308dd27aceb99099a1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L55-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e3524f474a095eee767d0e25e15fd0503517e43c80b0c8236fe1011b177b3a80:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L69-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0ec22dcd7da9d6f96fa6f90f714fe4f7c6f69059273f1777bd05c4e35fb4fe9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f8a03516efa84bb4ba37e1fd24d8f97f",
      "statement": "window_size_sentences and window_stride_sentences both default to 1, so each sentence is its own window. window_size_sentences sets how many sentences go into each source passage window; window_stride_sentences sets the stride between consecutive windows, and stride 1 produces overlapping windows.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L62-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9ab21960b2a97d1d0548c02415be2edab8ceb35033d536fc91d5f8cc60bc18e2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6e20ca1a45254efcba33c0960e1033fb",
      "statement": "The candidate-selection caps are max_candidates_lexical=200 (inverted-index seeds, or lexical prefilter hits on the fallback path), max_candidates_embedding=200 (embedding candidates added on top of index seeds), and max_candidates_total=400 (combined set after ranking by max(embedding_score, lexical_score), then capped before Smith-Waterman). Lexical scores are filled only for inverted-index seeds; embedding-only extras keep lexical_score=0.0 and rely on min_embedding_similarity to surface as retrieval_support.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1338-L1354",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a2042275e7aea0ecf343b786dcfbca39e973467aebee1e7aa668ef8e67bffda:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1357-L1373",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e9b2a144007f78dfb1e5d84fcb798493f5d28266a443fbb5140500b617a9414:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L65-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0ab658f2abbecb4bf0b019668ea3b31cd7d637b8c7a9a89bd2d91fd96af7d75b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a428d49b183b420e870a1d1784becc18",
      "statement": "A custom tokenizer or segmenter takes the lexical fallback path: PreparedCitationCorpus.from_sources leaves inverted_index=None and rust_corpus=None, and _select_candidates uses the lexical prefilter (plus optional embedding extras) instead of the inverted-index intersect. The public API and Smith-Waterman localization are unchanged on this path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1227-L1228",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f3018cccb56fc4c83abfae6e8e5f64a476b9f034cd81fa9601e76fb7e9cdbb96:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1292-L1335",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42c0bbefdca5682f9ffe278c5c3dcba0c586e4c796b84217bc1e2c0d4a8d836a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e6f3e048fec04267a77eece5c87201ff",
      "statement": "prefer_source_order controls the citation sort key after Smith-Waterman. When True (default) the tie-break order is earlier source_index, then earlier char_start, then longer evidence span, then candidate_index. When False it is earlier char_start, then longer evidence span, then source_index, then candidate_index. Citations are then deduplicated by (source_id, evidence_spans) tuple, capped per source by max_citations_per_source, and trimmed to top_k.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1523-L1550",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0941c75e7229f912c66590a2dc6339900ad275856f1c5643f833589af8453761:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1571-L1589",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7be18404e98e140082e00926d646303903b631097e54aca10b438e135a54dea4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L79-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2487af2adac6aca487ee4158aaf212b9a53ea7465f3f78539ac2ae4102e76b2a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a684a2fccb574c67a99b2e628104b432",
      "statement": "match_score (default 2), mismatch_score (default -1), and gap_score (default -1) are direct Smith-Waterman parameters that control the local-alignment score between an answer span and a candidate window. They are not weighted into the final citation score.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L765-L765",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:89b759ae9669b4620677977303587c5f3d5d116bdba6312f0e34a4fc2afb8331:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L75-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8a7639d18990f6afb86457a4d734380f604dc7da6feacaf3df44ef965dc9f73e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ffc5b4aabfc94902a55d10a97785f9e5",
      "statement": "CitationWeights defaults are alignment=1.0, answer_coverage=1.0, evidence_coverage=0.0, lexical=0.5, embedding=0.5. Weights are summed directly and are not normalized, so their absolute values matter. The embedding component is computed as weights.embedding * max(0.0, embedding_score), clipping negative embeddings before the weight is applied.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L808-L821",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:deb6b66ede4dfed1022481cea9c62b7d2836d8634ca663e0c0a63dcf9059d82a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L13-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0bade5ed1896e483b3a1e7c175965eff90ec4a835545bf5e1100c104b9df759e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b434346958dc418692d41ffba80b0846",
      "statement": "multi_span_evidence defaults to False and is the master switch for the multi-span evidence feature. multi_span_merge_gap_chars defaults to 16 and is the maximum source-character gap between two match regions before they are merged; merge_gap_chars <= 0 disables merging. multi_span_max_spans defaults to 5 and is the maximum number of spans per citation after merging; if exceeded, the citation falls back to a single contiguous span. The aligner runs return_match_blocks=True only when multi_span_evidence=True, and the Rust and Python backends produce identical evidence_spans and exact_evidence on this path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1384-L1425",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7567b3d59a9f0f6a255aae6cb088daf92a0761002949afd30e0288064eaf59a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1471-L1510",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c4560863fdece012d60ff2972de0419abd9e58bf3aa0f6bdedfcfda86632258:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L81-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:306e2cd0677b8d135125441bc3ecc45b48bc5649bb53c230fbb625a89f82b195:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_17e9c693710a47a98eda95fd9d40c653",
      "statement": "The contradiction check in check_contradiction runs over the full candidate passage (not the truncated Smith-Waterman evidence) and fires on negation mismatch, number mismatch, leftover n-gram slot, entity swap, and temporal or polarity mismatches. When it fires against the best-ranked citation, the span status is forced to \"partial\"; contradiction never produces \"unsupported\" because there is evidence, it just conflicts with the claim.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1592-L1607",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c95392171298b580ea68d065b5cc1d37971661cab38b2e1e9b115e5ba928dfc8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1621-L1632",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42e2d61bf44545e5b58d8109c1e13ef4c100c8e46561c9b99e3646b460f47748:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f3ef06393e3148f9b6e4b7526b06cae6",
      "statement": "The CitationConfig constructor rejects allow_embedding_only and supported_embedding_similarity as removed options and raises ValueError; the supported path for semantic retrieval signals is SpanCitations.retrieval_support, not an embedding-only Citation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L85-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d1b7e8c479b76b6466bb32646c345bb8514993301fa097043ce924e509150e27:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2a303b96abcf4804b6c28acccf5ac1a7",
      "statement": "When an embedder is passed, the candidate selector queries the inverted index first and then _add_embedding_candidates can add high-cosine-similarity passages the index may have missed. Those extras still go through Smith-Waterman. retrieval_support is not a Citation and never flips status. Rust prepare still runs with the embedder on the default SimpleTokenizer + SimpleSegmenter path; the embedding index is built on the prepared candidates.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1230-L1230",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1596e9714c0a4842413fe467736e131669689987c5dd8686ec078f3e2ab7609b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1338-L1354",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a2042275e7aea0ecf343b786dcfbca39e973467aebee1e7aa668ef8e67bffda:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9b232f6c97a84fe6bfa592264ceae8b2",
      "statement": "CitationConfig exposes four preset class methods: balanced() (identical to the default constructor: top_k=3, min_answer_coverage=0.2, supported_answer_coverage=0.6, min_final_score=0.0, min_embedding_similarity=0.3, max_candidates_lexical=200, max_candidates_embedding=200, max_candidates_total=400, max_citations_per_source=2, max_retrieval_support=3, require_all_answer_tokens_in_evidence=False), strict() (top_k=2, min_answer_coverage=0.4, supported_answer_coverage=0.7, min_final_score=0.3, max_citations_per_source=1, max_retrieval_support=2, require_all_answer_tokens_in_evidence=True), permissive() (top_k=5, min_answer_coverage=0.15, supported_answer_coverage=0.4, min_final_score=0.0, min_embedding_similarity=0.25, max_citations_per_source=3, max_retrieval_support=5; exact citations still require localized Smith-Waterman evidence and it does not emit embedding-only citations), and fast() (top_k=1, max_candidates_lexical=50, max_candidates_embedding=50, max_candidates_total=100, max_citations_per_source=1, max_retrieval_support=1).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L99-L198",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52447c725b8f738a8dc05b80542be95495f09ba2c85ace76200393eb239fe582:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_efe8b15d8d1c4a55a8d0e2ce3d9bbee5",
      "statement": "Structured field:value sources (Data2txt hours, amenities, business attributes) get a second Smith-Waterman pass per matching candidate with gap_score=0 on the answer text alone; prose candidates keep the configured gap penalty. Faithful rewrites can resolve to \"supported\" or \"partial\"; invented fields that do not match any field line stay \"unsupported\".",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1040-L1068",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e18d1a288f79b387836809d7ec3068c50923b0654af2fc3fcfba8dba1ad79469:"
        },
